From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: AMD's GPU services library for AMD-sponsored games (Wine
 patch 0978)

Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered said the graphics driver was below its
requirements, and The Last of Us Part II logged "Driver Supported: NO":
both ask AMD's GPU Services library (amd_ags_x64.dll, shipped with the
game) for the driver, which asks the Radeon driver the PS5 hasn't. Wine
patch 0978 adds Proton's builtin amd_ags_x64 (LGPL; AMD's amd_ags.h, MIT),
which answers from the Vulkan device with a current driver version and
passes AGS's Direct3D 11 and 12 extensions to DXVK and VKD3D-Proton,
without its Unix side (no libdrm on the PS5). The title overrides
amd_ags_x64 to builtin for it to replace a game's own copy.
