+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] amd_ags_x64: AMD's GPU services library, so AMD-sponsored
+ games see a driver.
+
+Games that AMD sponsored ship AMD's GPU Services library (amd_ags_x64.dll)
+and ask it for the driver: on Windows it asks the Radeon driver (ADL,
+atiadlxx.dll), which the PS5 hasn't, so it answers nothing. Marvel's
+Spider-Man Remastered then says the graphics driver is below its
+requirements, and The Last of Us Part II logs "Driver Supported: NO".
+
+This is Proton's builtin amd_ags_x64 (ValveSoftware/wine, by Paul Gofman
+and others for CodeWeavers, LGPL 2.1 or later; amd_ags.h is AMD's, MIT),
+which answers from the Vulkan device (the PS5's GPU is AMD's) with a
+current Radeon Software version, and passes AGS's Direct3D 11 and 12
+extensions to DXVK and VKD3D-Proton. Without a Unix side: the PS5 has no
+libdrm, so the GPU's units and clocks stay AGS's defaults.
+
+A game's own amd_ags_x64.dll still loads unless the title overrides it to
+builtin (PC5 does: its profiles' DLL overrides).
